OpenAI Token Usage Response Example

Below is an example that demonstrates how to extract and log token usage details from an OpenAI API response. In many applications that integrate with the OpenAI LLM APIs, it is important to monitor the tokens used in both prompt and completion portions. The example below shows how to parse the JSON response received after a request and extract values for prompt_tokens, completion_tokens, and total_tokens.

Make an API request to OpenAI and receive a response that includes token usage details.
Parse the JSON response.
Extract the "usage" object from the response.
Log or further process the individual token count values.
Below is a complete Node.js example using the native fetch API (supported in recent Node versions) to demonstrate how to perform these steps:

Code Example (JavaScript)
Copy
