Fallback Structure Code Example--

Below is a complete JavaScript code example demonstrating a fallback structure for calling LLM APIs. In this example, the code first attempts to get a response from a primary LLM API endpoint. If the primary call fails (for instance, due to network issues or an unexpected response), the code gracefully falls back to a secondary API endpoint. This pattern is common in robust systems where non-critical tasks require resilience and maximum uptime.

